    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The controller method is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110-138`).\n\n## Before the controller runs\n\n1. **Idempotency filter** (`IdempotentOwnerCreateFilter`) \u2014 if the request has an `Idempotency-Key` header seen before, it replays the cached response with **200** and never reaches the controller or DB. Otherwise it proceeds and caches the body afterward only if the response is 201.\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; non-admins get 403.\n3. **Bean Validation of the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 fails produce **400** via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with `' -` separators)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)` (optional)\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^\\d{4}$)` (optional)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(^[-+()\\d ]+$)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent` (optional)\n\n## Inside the controller, in execution order\n\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`), which triggers normalization side-effects via entity setters and the mapper:\n   - `registrationDate`: if null \u2192 `LocalDate.now()`, then rolled forward past weekends/2026 holidays (`BusinessDay`)\n   - `email` \u2192 lower-cased\n   - `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2192 trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, abbreviations expanded (`AddressNormalizer`)\n   - `telephone` \u2192 converted to E.164 (assumes +61, drops leading 0); invalid \u2192 throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**\n5. **Postcode-vs-city check** (`Postcode.isValidForCity`) \u2014 postcode outside the city's region range \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Disposable-email block** (`DisposableEmail.isBlocked`) \u2014 blocked domain \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Daily owner limit** (`DailyOwnerLimitException.rejectIfAtLimit`) \u2014 \u2265100 owners registered today \u2192 **429**.\n8. **Bulk-signup warning** (`BulkSignup.isWarning`) \u2014 >80 owners today \u2192 sets a boolean (not a rejection; applied to the response at step 17).\n9. **City capacity** (`CityAtCapacityException.rejectIfAtCapacity`) \u2014 \u226550 owners in the same normalized city \u2192 **409**.\n10. **Read `sharesHousehold` flag** from the DTO.\n11. **Identity-key duplicate check** (`IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate`) \u2014 same `telephone-digits|email|` as a non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` \u2192 **409**.\n12. **Household duplicate check** (`DuplicateHouseholdException.rejectIfDuplicate`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, matching `householdId` (SHA-256 of lastName+postcode) of a non-deleted owner \u2192 **409**.\n13. **Assign `customerCode`** (`UniqueCustomerCode.assign`) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` with `-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffix until unique. *(mutates owner)*\n14. **Set `namesakeCount`** (`Namesakes.count`) \u2014 count of owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive). *(mutates owner)*\n15. **Set `householdGold`** (`GoldTier.qualifies`) \u2014 true if household has \u22653 members. *(mutates owner)*\n16. **Possible-duplicate flagging** (`PossibleDuplicate.assign`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, if an existing owner shares postcode+lastName but a different phone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>`. *(mutates owner)*\n17. **Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`) \u2014 the DB insert, assigns the id. Entity-level `@NotEmpty` on `firstName`/`lastName`/`city`/`telephone` are the second validation layer here; a `DataIntegrityViolationException` maps to **404**.\n18. **Map entity \u2192 response DTO** (`ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`) \u2014 computes derived read-only fields (displayName, initials, householdId, membership number/points/level, locality, timezone, contactPreference, ageBand, checkDigit, selfLink, etc.).\n19. **Audit log** \u2014 an INFO line to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n20. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** on the response DTO (from step 8), set the `Location` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **`findAllOwners()` is called 8 times** (steps 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16) \u2014 eight full table reads per create.\n- **No `@Transactional` on the controller**, so the 8 reads and the write are separate transactions \u2014 the uniqueness/duplicate checks are **not atomic** with the insert (TOCTOU race under concurrent requests).\n- **No `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks** and **no custom `ConstraintValidator`s** \u2014 all the \"business\" validation is imperative in the controller.\n- No password hashing (owners have no password) and **no email/event dispatch** \u2014 the only effects beyond the DB insert are the audit log line and the in-memory idempotency cache.\n\nOne detail to double-check if it matters: the entity-level `@NotEmpty` failures surface as `DataIntegrityViolationException` mapped to **404**, which is an odd status for a validation failure \u2014 but that's what the current `ExceptionControllerAdvice` does."
